WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
Use only a clinician-agreed setup and load.
This example uses a light empty box.

00:06.000 --> 00:12.000
Watch a small lift, then controlled lowering.
Two hands are shown; your method may differ.

00:12.000 --> 00:18.000
Rest. This does not establish a safe heavy load.
Balance, grip and bone health need assessment.

00:18.000 --> 00:24.000
Example replay: a tabletop task rehearsal.
No carrying, overhead or floor lift is shown.

00:24.000 --> 00:30.000
Progression belongs in an individual plan.
Stop if pain, fatigue or balance changes.

00:30.000 --> 00:36.000
Final example: lower before releasing.
Use your agreed support and assistance.

00:36.000 --> 00:42.000
Consider a lighter load, assessed aid or help.
Do not test your limit from this video.
